# What is carried here and what is not turns on reproducibility, not on size.
#
# The simulation CSVs are carried despite being large. They are deterministic —
# `run_sim.py` and `diagnose_c3.py` produce byte-identical files — but that is a
# claim about this machine, and the point of carrying them is that someone can
# recompute every number in the write-up without owning a machine that reproduces
# our bytes. They are the only place `sim/` and `analysis/` meet.
#
# What follows is ignored because rerunning is not the issue: none of it is
# reproducible at all. A capture is of a network that no longer exists in that
# state, and raw tool output is an artifact of one run. Those are published as a
# release artifact, referenced by run id from `runs.ndjson`.
raw/
captures/

# Dry-run output is neither evidence nor irreplaceable: it is an apparatus check,
# regenerated by `run_block.py --dry-run` in seconds, and its records are stubbed.
dryrun.ndjson
dryrun-raw/
dryrun-stores/

# One history store per measured run, so that no run pays for another run's
# compaction inside its own wall clock.  Ignored for the same reason as `raw/`: each
# file is what one run wrote to a network that no longer exists in that state.  They
# are also, for the privileged conditions, owned by root.  Not ignoring them would be
# worse than untidy — `provenance.py` counts untracked files as a dirty tree, so the
# first real block would abort on the stores the block before it wrote.
stores/

# What the harness writes while it runs, and the pilot's copies of the same.
# `provenance.py` aborts a block on a dirty tree — modified files as well as untracked
# ones — so nothing the harness appends to during a block can be tracked while
# collection is running, or the second block aborts on the first block's output. The
# dry runs never hit this because they pass --allow-dirty; the first live block did.
# `runs.ndjson` is a deliverable and is added with `git add -f` once collection has
# ended, when the tree no longer has to stay clean under it.
runs.ndjson
collect.log
collect-status.json
collect-status.tmp
collect.launchd.out
collect.launchd.err
COLLECTION-STOPPED.txt
pilot.ndjson
pilot.log
pilot-status.json
pilot-status.tmp
PILOT-STOPPED.txt
pilot-raw/
pilot-captures/
pilot-stores/
pilot-settle/
